---
// Scroll-driven "cellulose factory" explainer — Apple-product-page style.
// Self-contained: scoped Astro <style> is fine here (everything lives inside
// this single component, not split across a page + markdown Content like
// notebook/[slug].astro), but scripts still run as a page-level <script> so
// GSAP registers once globally. Uses the project's existing npm `gsap`
// dependency (already imported/registered in BaseLayout.astro) — do not add
// a second copy from a CDN.
//
// ── Where to edit ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// - Captions/headlines: the `scenes` array markup below (search "Scene 0" … "Scene 6").
// - Colours: the --cena / --cex / --bgl custom properties near the top of <style>.
// - Chain lengths: the `data-count` attribute on each `.cf-chain` placeholder.
---

<section class="cf" id="cellulose-factory" aria-label="Animated explainer: how enzymes break down cellulose into glucose">

  <!-- Reduced-motion fallback lives in the DOM always; JS + CSS decide which mode shows -->
  <div class="cf-track">
    <div class="cf-viewport">
      <div class="cf-stage">

        <!-- Scene 0 — The raw material -->
        <div class="cf-scene" data-scene="0">
          <p class="cf-eyebrow">Cellulose degradation, step by step</p>
          <h3 class="cf-headline">Cellulose. A chain built to resist breaking down.</h3>
          <div class="cf-belt">
            <div class="cf-chain cf-chain--long" data-count="14" data-color="var(--fibre)"></div>
            <div class="cf-chain cf-chain--long cf-chain--ghost" data-count="14" data-color="var(--fibre)"></div>
            <div class="cf-chain cf-chain--long cf-chain--ghost2" data-count="14" data-color="var(--fibre)"></div>
          </div>
          <p class="cf-caption">Long chains of glucose, linked end to end and packed tightly together with dense hydrogen bonding — this is what a plant cell wall is mostly made of. Three different enzymes take turns pulling it apart. Meet the first.</p>
        </div>

        <!-- Scene 1 — Machine 1: Endoglucanase (CenA) -->
        <div class="cf-scene" data-scene="1">
          <p class="cf-eyebrow">Machine 1 — CenA (Endoglucanase)</p>
          <h3 class="cf-headline">It cuts in the middle.</h3>
          <div class="cf-belt">
            <div class="cf-chain cf-chain--cena" data-count="14" data-color="var(--cena)"></div>
            <div class="cf-machine cf-machine--cena">
              <span class="cf-machine-glow"></span>
              <span class="cf-machine-label">CenA</span>
            </div>
          </div>
          <p class="cf-caption">CenA, an endoglucanase, cleaves random bonds inside the chain, creating new free ends for the next machine to grab.</p>
        </div>

        <!-- Scene 2 — Machine 2: Exoglucanase (Cex) -->
        <div class="cf-scene" data-scene="2">
          <p class="cf-eyebrow">Machine 2 — Cex (Cellobiohydrolase)</p>
          <h3 class="cf-headline">It chews from the ends.</h3>
          <div class="cf-belt">
            <div class="cf-chain cf-chain--cex" data-count="8" data-color="var(--cena)"></div>
            <div class="cf-machine cf-machine--cex">
              <span class="cf-machine-glow"></span>
              <span class="cf-machine-label">Cex</span>
            </div>
            <div class="cf-output cf-output--cellobiose"></div>
          </div>
          <p class="cf-caption">Cex, a cellobiohydrolase, latches onto a chain end and walks along it, releasing two linked glucose units — cellobiose — one pair at a time.</p>
        </div>

        <!-- Scene 3 — Machine 3: β-Glucosidase -->
        <div class="cf-scene" data-scene="3">
          <p class="cf-eyebrow">Machine 3 — β-Glucosidase</p>
          <h3 class="cf-headline">It splits the last bond.</h3>
          <div class="cf-belt">
            <div class="cf-pair-feed"></div>
            <div class="cf-machine cf-machine--bgl">
              <span class="cf-machine-glow"></span>
              <span class="cf-machine-label">BGL</span>
            </div>
            <div class="cf-output cf-output--glucose"></div>
          </div>
          <p class="cf-caption">β-Glucosidase breaks the one remaining bond in cellobiose, releasing two separate glucose molecules.</p>
        </div>

        <!-- Scene 4 — The output -->
        <div class="cf-scene" data-scene="4">
          <p class="cf-eyebrow">The payoff</p>
          <h3 class="cf-headline">Glucose. Ready for fermentation.</h3>
          <div class="cf-bin-wrap">
            <div class="cf-bin"></div>
            <div class="cf-counter"><span class="cf-counter-num">0</span></div>
          </div>
          <p class="cf-caption">The smallest unit — a simple sugar that yeast and bacteria can ferment straight into fuel.</p>
        </div>

        <!-- Scene 5 — The problem: three separate machines -->
        <div class="cf-scene" data-scene="5">
          <p class="cf-eyebrow">The catch</p>
          <h3 class="cf-headline">Three separate machines. A long way to travel.</h3>
          <div class="cf-map">
            <div class="cf-map-machine cf-map-machine--cena">CenA</div>
            <div class="cf-map-machine cf-map-machine--cex">Cex</div>
            <div class="cf-map-machine cf-map-machine--bgl">BGL</div>
            <svg class="cf-map-paths" viewBox="0 0 600 260" preserveAspectRatio="none" aria-hidden="true">
              <path class="cf-path cf-path--1" d="M110,60 C220,20 260,140 320,120 S460,40 500,80" />
              <path class="cf-path cf-path--2" d="M110,200 C200,230 260,120 340,160 S470,200 500,160" />
            </svg>
            <div class="cf-lost-fragment cf-lost-fragment--1"></div>
            <div class="cf-lost-fragment cf-lost-fragment--2"></div>
            <div class="cf-pileup"></div>
          </div>
          <p class="cf-caption">Every intermediate has to drift through the cell, find the right enzyme, and bind it — by chance. Some wander. Some pile up waiting.</p>
        </div>

        <!-- Scene 6 — The 3-in-1 machine (the goal) -->
        <div class="cf-scene" data-scene="6">
          <p class="cf-eyebrow">The idea behind this project</p>
          <h3 class="cf-headline cf-headline--big">One machine. Every step. One place.</h3>
          <div class="cf-fusion">
            <div class="cf-fusion-chain" data-count="10" data-color="var(--fibre)"></div>
            <div class="cf-fusion-machine">
              <span class="cf-fusion-module cf-fusion-module--cena">CenA</span>
              <span class="cf-fusion-module cf-fusion-module--cex">Cex</span>
              <span class="cf-fusion-module cf-fusion-module--bgl">BGL</span>
            </div>
            <div class="cf-fusion-output"></div>
          </div>
          <p class="cf-caption cf-caption--big">Fuse the enzymes together and the intermediates never have to travel — no drifting, no searching, no waiting in line. That's the bet this project is testing.</p>
        </div>

      </div>

      <!-- Progress dots -->
      <div class="cf-dots" aria-hidden="true">
        <span class="cf-dot" data-dot="0"></span>
        <span class="cf-dot" data-dot="1"></span>
        <span class="cf-dot" data-dot="2"></span>
        <span class="cf-dot" data-dot="3"></span>
        <span class="cf-dot" data-dot="4"></span>
        <span class="cf-dot" data-dot="5"></span>
        <span class="cf-dot" data-dot="6"></span>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- Static fallback for prefers-reduced-motion: plain stacked cards, no JS needed -->
  <noscript>
    <div class="cf-static-note">Enable JavaScript to see the animated version of this explainer.</div>
  </noscript>
</section>

<script>
  import { gsap } from 'gsap';
  import { ScrollTrigger } from 'gsap/ScrollTrigger';
  import { MotionPathPlugin } from 'gsap/MotionPathPlugin';
  gsap.registerPlugin(ScrollTrigger, MotionPathPlugin);

  const root = document.getElementById('cellulose-factory');
  if (root) {
    const reduceMotion = window.matchMedia('(prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)').matches;

    // ── Build hexagon chains programmatically (avoids hand-writing hundreds of SVG nodes) ──
    function hexPoints(cx: number, cy: number, r: number) {
      const pts = [];
      for (let i = 0; i < 6; i++) {
        const a = (Math.PI / 180) * (60 * i - 30);
        pts.push(`${(cx + r * Math.cos(a)).toFixed(1)},${(cy + r * Math.sin(a)).toFixed(1)}`);
      }
      return pts.join(' ');
    }

    function buildChain(el: Element) {
      const count = parseInt(el.getAttribute('data-count') || '8', 10);
      const color = el.getAttribute('data-color') || 'var(--fibre)';
      const r = 15;
      const spacing = r * 1.7;
      const width = spacing * (count - 1) + r * 2 + 8;
      const height = r * 2 + 8;
      const cy = height / 2;
      let svg = `<svg viewBox="0 0 ${width} ${height}" class="cf-chain-svg" preserveAspectRatio="xMidYMid meet">`;
      for (let i = 0; i < count - 1; i++) {
        const x1 = r + 4 + i * spacing + r * 0.8;
        const x2 = r + 4 + (i + 1) * spacing - r * 0.8;
        svg += `<line x1="${x1}" y1="${cy}" x2="${x2}" y2="${cy}" stroke="${color}" stroke-width="3" class="cf-bond" data-bond="${i}"/>`;
      }
      for (let i = 0; i < count; i++) {
        const cx = r + 4 + i * spacing;
        svg += `<polygon points="${hexPoints(cx, cy, r)}" fill="${color}" fill-opacity="0.22" stroke="${color}" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linejoin="round" class="cf-hex" data-hex="${i}"/>`;
      }
      svg += `</svg>`;
      el.innerHTML = svg;
    }

    document.querySelectorAll('.cf-chain, .cf-fusion-chain').forEach(buildChain);

    // Small reusable pair (cellobiose: 2 hexagons) / single hexagon builders
    function buildPair(parent: Element, color = 'var(--cena)') {
      const r = 13;
      const w = r * 3.2, h = r * 2 + 6;
      const cy = h / 2;
      const el = document.createElement('div');
      el.className = 'cf-pair';
      el.innerHTML = `<svg viewBox="0 0 ${w} ${h}" class="cf-pair-svg">
        <line x1="${r*1.1}" y1="${cy}" x2="${w - r*1.1}" y2="${cy}" stroke="${color}" stroke-width="2.5"/>
        <polygon points="${hexPoints(r, cy, r)}" fill="${color}" fill-opacity="0.25" stroke="${color}" stroke-width="2" stroke-linejoin="round"/>
        <polygon points="${hexPoints(w - r, cy, r)}" fill="${color}" fill-opacity="0.25" stroke="${color}" stroke-width="2" stroke-linejoin="round"/>
      </svg>`;
      parent.appendChild(el);
      return el;
    }
    function buildSingle(parent: Element, color = 'var(--bgl)') {
      const r = 13;
      const w = r * 2 + 6, h = r * 2 + 6;
      const el = document.createElement('div');
      el.className = 'cf-single';
      el.innerHTML = `<svg viewBox="0 0 ${w} ${h}" class="cf-single-svg">
        <polygon points="${hexPoints(w/2, h/2, r)}" fill="${color}" fill-opacity="0.3" stroke="${color}" stroke-width="2" stroke-linejoin="round"/>
      </svg>`;
      parent.appendChild(el);
      return el;
    }

    if (reduceMotion) {
      // ── Reduced-motion fallback: static stacked scenes, no pinning/scrubbing ──
      root.classList.add('cf-reduced');
      document.querySelectorAll('.cf-pair-feed').forEach(el => buildPair(el));
      document.querySelectorAll('.cf-output--cellobiose').forEach(el => buildPair(el));
      document.querySelectorAll('.cf-output--glucose').forEach(el => { buildSingle(el); buildSingle(el); });
    } else {
      const scenes = Array.from(root.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('.cf-scene'));
      const dots = Array.from(root.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('.cf-dot'));
      gsap.set(scenes, { autoAlpha: 0 });
      gsap.set(scenes[0], { autoAlpha: 1 });
      dots[0]?.classList.add('is-active');

      const N = scenes.length; // 7
      const tl = gsap.timeline({
        scrollTrigger: {
          trigger: '.cf-track',
          start: 'top top',
          end: 'bottom bottom',
          scrub: 0.6,
          pin: '.cf-viewport',
          onUpdate: self => {
            const idx = Math.min(N - 1, Math.round(self.progress * (N - 1)));
            dots.forEach((d, i) => d.classList.toggle('is-active', i === idx));
          },
        },
        defaults: { ease: 'none' },
      });

      // Crossfades between scenes, evenly spaced across the timeline (unit = 1 per scene)
      for (let i = 0; i < N; i++) {
        const t = i; // start time of this scene's "hold"
        if (i > 0) {
          tl.to(scenes[i - 1], { autoAlpha: 0, duration: 0.25 }, t - 0.25);
          tl.to(scenes[i], { autoAlpha: 1, duration: 0.25 }, t - 0.25);
        }
      }

      // Scene 0 — chain drifts in, ghost chains parallax behind it
      const chain0 = root.querySelector('.cf-chain--long:not(.cf-chain--ghost):not(.cf-chain--ghost2)');
      const ghost1 = root.querySelector('.cf-chain--ghost');
      const ghost2 = root.querySelector('.cf-chain--ghost2');
      if (chain0) tl.fromTo(chain0, { x: -80, autoAlpha: 0 }, { x: 0, autoAlpha: 1, duration: 0.8 }, 0);
      if (ghost1) tl.fromTo(ghost1, { x: -40, autoAlpha: 0 }, { x: 0, autoAlpha: 0.4, duration: 0.8 }, 0.05);
      if (ghost2) tl.fromTo(ghost2, { x: -120, autoAlpha: 0 }, { x: 0, autoAlpha: 0.25, duration: 0.8 }, 0.1);

      // Scene 1 — paced in three beats: chain settles, then the machine makes an
      // entrance (not just a quick fade), then it cuts. Gives Scene 0 -> Scene 1
      // room to breathe instead of popping the machine in immediately.
      const cenaChain = root.querySelector('.cf-chain--cena');
      const cenaMachine = root.querySelector('.cf-machine--cena');
      if (cenaChain && cenaMachine) {
        tl.fromTo(cenaMachine,
          { autoAlpha: 0, scale: 0.7, x: -50 },
          { autoAlpha: 1, scale: 1, x: 0, duration: 0.3, ease: 'back.out(1.6)' },
          1.05);

        // Cut at two internal bonds (indices 4 and 9, out of 14 hexagons), then
        // actually separate the three resulting pieces — otherwise this just
        // shows two thin gaps in what still reads as one continuous chain.
        // All of this has to land before 1.75, where the crossfade into Scene 2
        // starts, or the split reads as unfinished mid-transition.
        const bySelector = (sel: string) => Array.from(cenaChain.querySelectorAll(sel));
        const cutBonds = bySelector('[data-bond="4"], [data-bond="9"]');
        const fragB = [...bySelector('[data-hex="5"],[data-hex="6"],[data-hex="7"],[data-hex="8"],[data-hex="9"]'),
                       ...bySelector('[data-bond="5"],[data-bond="6"],[data-bond="7"],[data-bond="8"]')];
        const fragC = [...bySelector('[data-hex="10"],[data-hex="11"],[data-hex="12"],[data-hex="13"]'),
                       ...bySelector('[data-bond="10"],[data-bond="11"],[data-bond="12"]')];

        tl.to(cutBonds, { opacity: 0, duration: 0.1 }, 1.4);
        tl.to(fragB, { x: 14, duration: 0.2, ease: 'power2.out' }, 1.45);
        tl.to(fragC, { x: 30, duration: 0.2, ease: 'power2.out' }, 1.45);
      }

      // Scene 2 — Cex machine "walks" the chain end, pairs peel off into cellobiose output
      const cexMachine = root.querySelector('.cf-machine--cex');
      const cexOutput = root.querySelector('.cf-output--cellobiose');
      if (cexMachine && cexOutput) {
        tl.fromTo(cexMachine, { autoAlpha: 0, x: -20 }, { autoAlpha: 1, x: 0, duration: 0.3 }, 2.1);
        for (let p = 0; p < 3; p++) {
          const pairEl = buildPair(cexOutput, 'var(--cena)');
          gsap.set(pairEl, { opacity: 0, y: -10 });
          tl.to(pairEl, { opacity: 1, y: 0, duration: 0.18 }, 2.35 + p * 0.18);
        }
      }

      // Scene 3 — cellobiose pair arrives, BGL splits it into two glucose
      const pairFeed = root.querySelector('.cf-pair-feed');
      const bglMachine = root.querySelector('.cf-machine--bgl');
      const glucoseOutput = root.querySelector('.cf-output--glucose');
      if (pairFeed && bglMachine && glucoseOutput) {
        const feedPair = buildPair(pairFeed, 'var(--cena)');
        tl.fromTo(feedPair, { autoAlpha: 0 }, { autoAlpha: 1, duration: 0.2 }, 3.1);
        tl.fromTo(bglMachine, { autoAlpha: 0, scale: 0.85 }, { autoAlpha: 1, scale: 1, duration: 0.25 }, 3.25);
        tl.to(feedPair, { autoAlpha: 0, duration: 0.15 }, 3.55);
        const g1 = buildSingle(glucoseOutput, 'var(--bgl)');
        const g2 = buildSingle(glucoseOutput, 'var(--bgl)');
        gsap.set([g1, g2], { opacity: 0 });
        tl.to(g1, { opacity: 1, x: -10, duration: 0.15 }, 3.6);
        tl.to(g2, { opacity: 1, x: 10, duration: 0.15 }, 3.65);
      }

      // Scene 4 — glucose drops into bin, counter ticks
      const counter = root.querySelector('.cf-counter-num');
      const bin = root.querySelector('.cf-bin');
      if (counter && bin) {
        const counterObj = { v: 0 };
        tl.fromTo(bin, { autoAlpha: 0, y: 12 }, { autoAlpha: 1, y: 0, duration: 0.25 }, 4.1);
        tl.to(counterObj, {
          v: 42, duration: 0.6, snap: 'v',
          onUpdate: () => { (counter as HTMLElement).textContent = String(Math.round(counterObj.v)); },
        }, 4.2);
      }

      // Scene 5 — zoom to factory map, fragments drift along winding paths, one pile forms
      const path1 = root.querySelector('.cf-path--1') as SVGPathElement | null;
      const path2 = root.querySelector('.cf-path--2') as SVGPathElement | null;
      const lost1 = root.querySelector('.cf-lost-fragment--1');
      const lost2 = root.querySelector('.cf-lost-fragment--2');
      const pileup = root.querySelector('.cf-pileup');
      if (path1 && lost1) {
        const len = path1.getTotalLength();
        gsap.set(lost1, { motionPath: { path: path1, align: path1 } });
        tl.fromTo(lost1, { autoAlpha: 0 }, { autoAlpha: 1, duration: 0.1 }, 5.1);
        tl.to(lost1, { motionPath: { path: path1, align: path1, alignOrigin: [0.5, 0.5] }, duration: 0.7, ease: 'power1.inOut' }, 5.15);
      }
      if (path2 && lost2) {
        tl.fromTo(lost2, { autoAlpha: 0 }, { autoAlpha: 1, duration: 0.1 }, 5.2);
        tl.to(lost2, { motionPath: { path: path2, align: path2, alignOrigin: [0.5, 0.5] }, duration: 0.65, ease: 'power1.inOut' }, 5.25);
      }
      if (pileup) {
        tl.fromTo(pileup, { scale: 0, autoAlpha: 0 }, { scale: 1, autoAlpha: 1, duration: 0.3, ease: 'back.out(1.7)' }, 5.6);
      }

      // Scene 6 — three machines slide together and fuse; chain flows through in one pass
      const modules = root.querySelectorAll('.cf-fusion-module');
      const fusionChain = root.querySelector('.cf-fusion-chain');
      const fusionOutput = root.querySelector('.cf-fusion-output');
      if (modules.length) {
        tl.fromTo(modules[0], { x: -70, autoAlpha: 0 }, { x: 0, autoAlpha: 1, duration: 0.3 }, 6.05);
        tl.fromTo(modules[1], { x: 0, autoAlpha: 0 }, { autoAlpha: 1, duration: 0.3 }, 6.1);
        tl.fromTo(modules[2], { x: 70, autoAlpha: 0 }, { x: 0, autoAlpha: 1, duration: 0.3 }, 6.15);
      }
      if (fusionChain) tl.fromTo(fusionChain, { x: -60, autoAlpha: 0 }, { x: 0, autoAlpha: 1, duration: 0.3 }, 6.3);
      if (fusionOutput) {
        const s1 = buildSingle(fusionOutput, 'var(--bgl)');
        const s2 = buildSingle(fusionOutput, 'var(--bgl)');
        const s3 = buildSingle(fusionOutput, 'var(--bgl)');
        gsap.set([s1, s2, s3], { opacity: 0 });
        tl.to([s1, s2, s3], { opacity: 1, stagger: 0.1, duration: 0.2 }, 6.55);
      }
    }
  }
</script>

<style>
  /* ── Palette: one accent per enzyme machine ─────────────────────── */
  .cf {
    --fibre: #8fa89c;
    --cena: #4f8fe8;
    --cex: #e8954f;
    --bgl: #a35fe8;
    --cf-bg: var(--c-bg);
    --cf-surface: var(--c-surface);
  }
  :global([data-theme="dark"]) .cf {
    --fibre: #7a9589;
    --cena: #6fa6f2;
    --cex: #f0a868;
    --bgl: #b87cf0;
  }

  .cf { position: relative; background: var(--cf-bg); }

  /* ── Scroll track + pinned viewport ──────────────────────────────── */
  .cf-track { position: relative; height: 700vh; }
  .cf-viewport {
    height: 100vh;
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    overflow: hidden;
  }
  .cf-stage { position: relative; width: min(900px, 92vw); height: min(560px, 76vh); }

  .cf-scene {
    position: absolute;
    inset: 0;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    text-align: center;
    gap: var(--sp-5);
  }

  .cf-eyebrow {
    font-size: 0.78rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: 0.1em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--c-text-muted);
    margin: 0;
  }
  .cf-headline {
    font-size: clamp(1.4rem, 4vw, 2.1rem);
    color: var(--c-secondary);
    margin: 0;
    line-height: 1.2;
  }
  .cf-headline--big { font-size: clamp(1.6rem, 4.5vw, 2.5rem); }
  .cf-caption {
    max-width: 52ch;
    font-size: 0.98rem;
    color: var(--c-text-muted);
    line-height: 1.6;
    margin: 0;
  }
  .cf-caption--big { font-size: 1.05rem; max-width: 56ch; }

  /* ── Belt / chain elements ────────────────────────────────────────── */
  .cf-belt { position: relative; width: 100%; height: 110px; display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; }
  .cf-chain, .cf-fusion-chain { display: inline-block; }
  /* These SVGs are built at runtime via innerHTML (see <script> below), so they never
     get Astro's scope attribute — :global() is required or these rules silently no-op. */
  :global(.cf-chain-svg) { height: 60px; width: auto; display: block; overflow: visible; }
  .cf-chain--long { position: absolute; }
  .cf-chain--ghost { opacity: 0.4; transform: translateY(18px) scale(0.92); }
  .cf-chain--ghost2 { opacity: 0.25; transform: translateY(-18px) scale(0.85); }

  .cf-machine {
    position: relative;
    width: 86px; height: 86px;
    border-radius: 18px;
    display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center;
    margin-left: var(--sp-6);
    background: var(--cf-surface);
    border: 2px solid currentColor;
  }
  .cf-machine--cena { color: var(--cena); }
  .cf-machine--cex { color: var(--cex); }
  .cf-machine--bgl { color: var(--bgl); }
  .cf-machine-glow {
    position: absolute; inset: 14px;
    border-radius: 50%;
    background: currentColor;
    opacity: 0.35;
    filter: blur(6px);
  }
  .cf-machine-label {
    position: relative;
    font-weight: 800;
    font-size: 0.82rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.04em;
    color: currentColor;
  }

  .cf-output, .cf-pair-feed { display: flex; gap: var(--sp-2); align-items: center; margin-left: var(--sp-6); min-width: 90px; min-height: 40px; }
  :global(.cf-pair-svg), :global(.cf-single-svg) { height: 36px; width: auto; display: block; }

  /* ── Bin / counter (Scene 4) ──────────────────────────────────────── */
  .cf-bin-wrap { display: flex; flex-direction: column; align-items: center; gap: var(--sp-3); }
  .cf-bin {
    width: 120px; height: 70px;
    border: 3px solid var(--bgl);
    border-top: none;
    border-radius: 0 0 14px 14px;
    background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--bgl) 10%, transparent);
  }
  .cf-counter-num {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 2.2rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    color: var(--bgl);
  }

  /* ── Factory map (Scene 5) ────────────────────────────────────────── */
